# Legacy filename entry points from the old PHP portfolio.
# Note: Cloudflare Pages treats `#` in `_redirects` as a comment character,
# so hash-anchor rules like `/#about /about 301` are (a) never triggered by
# real HTTP requests (browsers strip the hash before sending) and (b) parsed
# incorrectly by Cloudflare into a broken `/` -> `/about` redirect. Do not
# add hash-anchor rules to this file.
/index               /                301
/index.html          /                301
/index.php           /                301

# Do NOT add a www -> apex rule here. Cloudflare Pages matches only the PATH in
# the source column, so an absolute `https://www.example.com/*` source is read as
# a path, never matches, and is dropped silently (verified: www served 200, not 301).
# Host-level redirects must live in the Cloudflare dashboard: Rules -> Redirect
# Rules, via the "Redirect from WWW to root" template (`https://www.*` ->
# `https://${1}`, 301). That rule is the ONLY thing enforcing www -> apex.
# See DEPLOYMENT.md step 3.
